      "text": "To find the value of \\( t \\) in the polynomial \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) with roots \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\), we can use Vieta's formulas effectively. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFirst, let's denote the roots of the polynomial \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) as:\n\\[\na, \\quad b, \\quad c.\n\\]\n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, for the polynomial \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\):\n1. The sum of the roots is given by:\n   \\[\n   a + b + c = -r.\n   \\]\n\n2. The sum of the product-to-sum pairs of the roots is given by:\n   \\[\n   ab + bc + ca = s.\n   \\]\n\n3. The product of the roots taken three at a time is given by:\n   \\[\n   abc = -t.\n   \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the roots of the polynomial \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\). According to the problem, these roots are \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\).\n\nTo find \\( t \\), we need:\n- The product of these roots:\n  \\[\n  (a+b)(b+c)(c+a).\n  \\]\n\nWe can expand this product using the identity for the product of roots:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = ab \\cdot (b+c) + ac \\cdot (b+c) + bc \\cdot (b+c) + (a+b)(b+c)(c+a).\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate each pair product:\n\\[\nab \\cdot (b+c) = ab^2 + abc,\n\\]\n\\[\nac \\cdot (b+c) = ac^2 + abc,\n\\]\n\\[\nbc \\cdot (b+c) = b^2c + b^2c = 2b^2c.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute these into the expanded form:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = ab^2 + abc + ac^2 + abc + 2b^2c = ab^2 + ac^2 + 2abc + 2b^2c.\n\\]\n\nUsing the identity for the product of roots from Vieta's formulas:\n\\[\nabc = -t.\n\\]\n\nNow differentiate both sides of \\( a+b+c = -r \\) with respect to \\( x \\):\n\\[\n1 = -r \\implies r = -1.\n\\]\n\nFrom Vieta’s results for \\( r \\):\n\\[\nr = -a-b-c \\implies 1 = -(-a-b-c) \\implies 1 = a+b+c.\n\\]\n\nThus, the constant term \\( t \\) satisfies:\n\\[\nabc = -t \\implies -t = abc.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( t \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-7}.\n\\]",
